VM1 - Kali
VM2 - Splunk
VM3 - windows server
VM4 - Wazuh

Specs for each VM:
VM name               RAM                storage             processors
kali                  2GB                80.1GB              2
splunk                4GB                60GB                2
wazuh                 3GB                60GB                2
windows server        4GB                60GB                2

kali intital configuration:
1) Set the static IP - 
sudo nano /etc/network/interfaces (opens up network config editor)

auto eth0
iface eth0 inet static
  address 192.168.100.50
  netmask 255.255.255.0
  gateway 192.168.100.2
  dns-nameservers 8.8.8.8
(Add static IP, subnet mask, gateway and dns nameserver and save)
2) Restart network-
sudo systemctl restart networking
3) Verify network connectivity with (ip a) and (ping 8.8.8.8). Ping must show responses.

Splunk initial configuration:
1) Install ubuntu server and set hostname, servername, username and password of your choice.
2) When terminal opens, login with your credentials.
3) Now set the static IP -
sudo nano /etc/netplan/00-installer-config.yaml (opens up the network config file)

network:
  version: 2
  ethernets:
    ens33:
      addresses:
        - 192.168.100.10/24
      routes:
        - to: default
          via: 192.168.100.2
      nameservers:
        addresses: [8.8.8.8]
(Add static IP, gateway and dns nameserver and save)
4) Restart the network -
sudo netplan apply
5) Verify network connectivity with (ip a) and (ping 8.8.8.8). Ping must show responses.
6) Splunk installation:
   - Go to https://www.splunk.com/en_us/download/splunk-enterprise.html and create a splunk account for free. 
   - After you create the account, verify email . After that, choose the installation package. Since we are in ubuntu server, choose linux to get a wget link under .deb.
     Example:wget -O splunk-10.4.0-f798d4d4908234-linux-amd64.deb "https://download.splunk.com/products/splunk/releases/10.4.0/linux/splunk-10.4.0-f798d4d4908234-linux-amd64.deb"
     Copy that wget command from splunk and paste it directly into ubuntu server to start downloading.
   - sudo dpkg -i splunk-10.4.0-f798d4d4908234-linux-amd64.deb (installation command)
   - set admin username and password: sudo /opt/splunk/bin/splunk start --accept-license
   - If the above one doesn't work: sudo /opt/splunk/bin/splunk start --accept-license --answer-yes --run-as-root
   - Enable splunk to start on boot: sudo /opt/splunk/bin/splunk enable boot-start --run-as-root
   - Splunk will be running. To open, splunk on browser, go to http://192.168.100.10:8000 (192.168.100.10 is splunk's IP address).

Wazuh initial configuration:
1) Install ubuntu server and set hostname, servername, username and password of your choice.
2) When terminal opens, login with your credentials.
3) Now set the static IP -
sudo nano /etc/netplan/00-installer-config.yaml (opens up the network config file)

network:
  version: 2
  ethernets:
    ens33:
      addresses:
        - 192.168.100.30/24
      routes:
        - to: default
          via: 192.168.100.2
      nameservers:
        addresses: [8.8.8.8]
(Add static IP, gateway and dns nameserver and save)
4) Restart the network -
sudo netplan apply
5) Verify network connectivity with (ip a) and (ping 8.8.8.8). Ping must show responses.
6) Wazuh manager installation:
   - Run these commands one by one:
     curl -s https://packages.wazuh.com/key/GPG-KEY-WAZUH | sudo gpg --no-default-keyring --keyring gnupg-ring:/usr/share/keyrings/wazuh.gpg --import && sudo chmod 644 /usr/share/keyrings/wazuh.gpg
     echo "deb [signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/wazuh.gpg] https://packages.wazuh.com/4.x/apt/ stable main" | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/wazuh.list
     sudo apt update && sudo apt install wazuh-manager -y
7) Start and enable wazuh manager:
   sudo systemctl start wazuh-manager
   sudo systemctl enable wazuh-manager
8) Verify if wazuh is running:
   sudo systemctl status wazuh-manager


Windows server initial configuration:
Use the windows server 2022 standard evaluation desktop experience. We can get a free trial to use up to 180 days.
1) Set static IP and DNS:
New-NetIPAddress -InterfaceAlias "Ethernet0" -IPAddress 192.168.100.20 -PrefixLength 24 -DefaultGateway 192.168.100.2
Set-DnsClientServerAddress -InterfaceAlias "Ethernet0" -ServerAddresses 8.8.8.8
2) Test connectivity:
ping 8.8.8.8 . This ping must return a response.

Final connectivity test:
Power on all 4 VMs and then from Kali Linux, run pings:
ping 192.168.100.10 (Splunk)
ping 192.168.100.20 (Windows server)
ping 192.168.100.30 (Wazuh)
From windows server, 
ping 192.168.100.50 (kali)
- Sometimes 192.168.100.20 ping from kali may fail. This is because windows firewall is blocking ping by default. 
netsh advfirewall firewall add rule name="Allow ICMPv4" protocol=icmpv4:8,any dir=in action=allow
This command turns off firewall. 

All pings must succeed.
